    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nFor sale by online auction on Friday 30th October 2026 at 2pm. (Unless previously sold).\n\nAccess to legal documents or to register to bid is available via the following link; https://osullivanhurley.dngauctions.ie/lot/details/d2d071ec-3938-41c6-8756-785ba4fc5503\n\nSet on a secluded 0.23 hectare (0.57 acre) site at the end of a quiet local road, this traditional stone-built cottage is located in Glenmore, approximately 4km from Kilmihil village. Surrounded by farmland, forestry and private homes, the property enjoys a peaceful rural setting with excellent renovation potential.\n\nAccommodation comprises an open-plan living/dining/kitchen with solid fuel stove, two bedrooms, one with walk-in wardrobe and en-suite, and a main bathroom. While requiring cosmetic upgrading and modernisation, the cottage offers an excellent opportunity to create a home to the purchaser's own style and requirements.\n\nTo the outside is an array of traditional stone-built outbuildings and a hay barn. Although requiring repair, these buildings offer considerable potential for storage, workshop or other uses, subject to any necessary planning permission. Mains electricity is connected, with a septic tank on site.\n\nKilmihil offers a range of everyday amenities including shops, schools, pharmacy, medical, sporting and community facilities. Ennis and Kilrush are also within easy reach, making the property suitable for those seeking a tranquil countryside setting while remaining accessible to larger urban centres.\n\nWith its private setting, traditional character and renovation potential, this property presents an attractive opportunity for a permanent home or countryside retreat.\n\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by prior appointment with sole selling agents. PSL 002295."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Dining Kitchen - 7.7m x 4.4m\nLiving Area - Traditional timber flooring, front aspect window, solid fuel stove with brick surround, door to bedroom one and open access to kitchen.Kitchen - Tile flooring, front and rear aspect windows, built-in wall and base units with tile splash back, space for fridge freezer and washing machine, integrated oven and extractor hood and fan, stairs leading to bedroom two.\n\nMain Bathroom - 3.3m x 1.95m\nTile flooring, rear aspect window, low level wc, wash hand basin and corner bath unit with tile splash back.\n\nBedroom One En-Suite - 4.55m x 2.95m\nTimber flooring, front aspect window, door to walk-in storage wardrobe and door to en-suite.\n\nEn-Suite - 2.55m x 1.44m\nTile flooring, rear aspect window, low level wc, wash hand basin and corner shower area with tile surround.\n\nBedroom Two - \nTimber flooring and two velux windows to the rear.\n\nDetached Shed - 8.55m x 3.9m\nLarge open plan area with potential.\n\nOutside - \nGravel driveway with outbuildings to the side and rear, unlandscaped but there was an enclosed garden area in the past to the rear.\n\n"
      },
